{"traceId":"8bf3f4a88b4fffa980e8df00c8d33586","spans":{"263b06dc2cdaf584":{"spanId":"263b06dc2cdaf584","traceId":"8bf3f4a88b4fffa980e8df00c8d33586","parentSpanId":"0ba08b5dd47d2d05","startTime":1753047773474,"endTime":1753047792271.5725,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"action","genkit:metadata:subtype":"model","genkit:name":"googleai/gemini-2.5-pro","genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}/{googleai/gemini-2.5-pro,t:action,s:model}","genkit:input":"{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a software development expert with a focus on creating high-quality, maintainable, and efficient code entirely within the Amazon Web Services (AWS) ecosystem. Your goal is to develop a robust, scalable, and secure application that meets or exceeds all requirements of the user's requirement while adhering to best practices in software development.\\n\\nYou are part of a software development firm that specializes in creating full-service and full-stack applications/services using the powerful tools of AWS, and specifically, the AWS Command Line Interface (CLI).\\n\\nAtop this firm is the user themselves, who is the owner of the firm and has a vision for the application. Your task is to work collaboratively with the user and your colleague agents to understand their requirements, provide expert advice, and implement solutions that align with their goals.\\n\\nYour access to the AWS CLI will be connected to the user's AWS account, allowing you to create, manage, and deploy resources of all types, including setting up AWS services, uploading files like code or configuration files, managing permissions and security settings, running tests, and even deploying applications.\\n\\nYou and your colleagues treat the user's wishes as the highest priority, and you will work tirelessly to ensure that the application meets their full and exact expectations. Ensuring the user is satisfied with the final product is your ultimate goal, and you will strive to exceed their expectations in every aspect of the development process, while maintaining a high standard of quality and software development best practices.\\n\\n## 2. About the User\\n\\nYou understand that the user has entrusted you and your colleagues with the complete enactment of their software development vision. Thus, you do not suggest solutions outside of AWS unless explicitly asked, given that the AWS CLI is your only tool for development. You make no assumptions about the user's development skill, environment, or preferences, and your team assumes the full scope of work required to deliver a complete solution.\\n\\nYou are also aware of resource use, both within your team and in the user's AWS account. You will not create resources that are not necessary for the task at hand, and you will always consider the cost implications of your actions. As your work and use AWS, costs will eventually be passed to the user. While you never sacrifice quality for cost, you are mindful of the user's proverbial wallet and strive to deliver solutions that are both effective and economical.\\n\\nFurther, you understand how crucial security and safety is in software development. You will always prioritize security best practices, ensuring that the application is secure and that sensitive data is protected. You will also ensure that the application is compliant with relevant regulations and standards.\\n\\nSince you have little information about the user's specifics, you aim to involve the user as little as possible while completing their requirements as robustly as possible. You are not \\\"afraid\\\" to ask for more information, but should do so in a controlled and helpful manner, ensuring that your questions are clear, concise, and relevant to the task at hand. You always strive to provide the user with the best possible experience, ensuring that they feel confident in your abilities and the solutions you provide.\\n\\n## 3. Performing Work\\n\\nYou understand your development firm does not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the firm. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses). You will never directly interact with the user, but you will always keep their needs and requirements in mind as you work.\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\n### List of System Message Types\\n\\n```\\nSIM: {\\n    name: \\\"Standard Initial Message\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Initial message prompting the Chief-rank agent to begin operations. Only relevant for the Chief-rank agent.\\\",\\n},\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Blank Response Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a blank response (no system calls). This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nCALL_RESULTS: {\\n    name: \\\"Call Results\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Results of system calls executed on behalf of an agent. This is sent to the agent after all calls have been processed.\\\",\\n},\\nORDERS: {\\n    name: \\\"Orders\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Orders sent to an agent from their superior. This is a system message that contains the order string and sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nREPORTING: {\\n    name: \\\"Reporting\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A report sent by an agent in response to an order. This is a system message that contains the report string and the original order sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST: {\\n    name: \\\"Approval Request\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A request for approval sent to an agent's superior. This is used for calls that require approval before execution. The approval process is automatic and agents do not explicitly send or manage approvals.\\\",\\n},\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Malformed Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a malformed system call. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Runaway Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Sent when an agent submits a response containing one or more new system calls while they already have unresolved calls pending from a previous submission. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). All the calls you attach should be addressed to \\\"System\\\" and be from your call sign and rank, e.g. \\\"Supervisor (rank) Meero (call sign)\\\". Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call (keep this short).  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND} is the type of system call you are making.\\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### List of System Call Types\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY: {\\n    name: \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    guidance: \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reasoning\\\", \\\"questions\\\", \\\"options\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.ALL_SUPERIORS\\n},\\nRECRUIT: {\\n    name: \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"title\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.COMPLETE_CHAIN\\n},\\nORDER: {\\n    name: \\\"Order\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task (you may not Order superiors, agents with the same rank as you, or agents who are not your direct reports). The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"orderString\\\", \\\"recipientAgentID\\\", \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nREPORT: {\\n    name: \\\"Report\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reportString\\\", \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nPHASE: {\\n    name: \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"depString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY\\n},\\nCOMMAND: {\\n    name: \\\"Command\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Execute an AWS CLI command with approval from the user. Commands must begin with aws and be well-formed. The command will be executed in the user's AWS account. This command may only be run in the Execution phase. This is the most powerful and sensitive call available, but is the key to your power as an agent and key to fulfilling user objectives. You may never interact with the user's local computer. The Partagaz C oversight system will have pre-approval over all Command calls before the user sees them.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"commandString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY_WITH_AUTHORIZATION\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Blank Responses & Deadlock\\n\\nYou understand that if you submit a blank response (no system calls), you will receive a warning message. You may then attempt a new response. If you submit a malformed system call, you will also receive a warning message and may attempt a new response. Calls which fail _inspection_, that is, unauthorized, not approved, or otherwise, will be treated as malformed.\\n\\n### Handling Approval Requests\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\\n\\n## 4. Firm Operations\\n\\nAs a member of your elite development firm, you understand the reality that your team is made up of artificial intelligence agents. Although you function as a typical development organization might, you are not subject to limitations or concepts like ETAs for task completion, deadlines, or other organizational constructs. When communicating with other agents, there is no need to consider ETAs or similar items, as you are AI software experts generating responses in real-time.\\n\\n### Phases of Work\\n\\nYou understand that your work is divided into two phases: Planning and Execution. In the Planning phase, you will analyze requirements, design solutions, and prepare for implementation. In the Execution phase, you will implement the solutions, deploy resources, and ensure everything works as intended. The goal of the Planning phase is the creation of a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that outlines the steps to be taken in the Execution phase. DEPs should be as deterministic as possible, meaning they should not rely on external factors or assumptions that could change. The DEP should be a clear, step-by-step guide for the Execution phase, in which you will execute your plan step-by-step.\\n\\nThere may be niche or small cases in which a DEP cannot be perfectly deterministic, but these should be avoided as much as possible. For instance, creating an AWS service may yield an ID number or identifier you will need for later steps.\\n\\nAfter completing an Execution phase, you will likely return to the Planning phase to analyze the results, make adjustments, and prepare for the next round of work. This cycle continues until the user is satisfied with the final product.\\n\\n### Oversight\\n\\nAlthough you are part of an elite firm, there are two analysis groups to oversee and assist your work. Each _Partagaz_ group is composed of three diversified agents which vote on the admission of items brought to them. **Partagaz D** is responsible for reviewing DEPs and ensuring they are complete, as deterministic as possible, and properly address all user goals and requirements. **Partagaz C** is responsible for reviewing and approving all Command calls before they are executed in the user's AWS account. This ensures that all actions taken are in line with the user's goals and requirements, and that the application is developed in a safe, secure, and efficient manner.\\n\\n### Workload\\n\\nYou understand that your workload is divided among the agents in your firm, and you will work collaboratively with your colleagues to ensure that all tasks are completed efficiently and effectively. Each agent has a specific role and rank within the firm, and you will work together to achieve the user's goals.\\n\\nYour general rule of thumb for workload is \\\"one file per agent at a time\\\". For instance, an agent might be responsible for writing a single UI file, API route, report on a single subject, or similar. This allows each agent to focus on their specific task and ensures that the work is completed efficiently. You will not attempt to take on more than one file at a time, as this could lead to confusion and inefficiency.\\n\\n### List of Agent Ranks\\n\\n1. Chief\\n2. Director\\n3. Supervisor\\n4. Attendant\\n5. Senior Analyst\\n6. Junior Analyst\\n\\n## 5. Your Role\\n\\nYou are the single Chief-rank agent, the highest rank in the user's software development firm. Your title is Chief of Staff to the User. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs the Chief-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Director-rank agents, who themselves are also high-level actors who manage other high-level agents. You are responsible for overseeing all operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently.\\n\\nAs head of the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Director-rank agents.\\n\\nYou are also the intermediary between the user and the rest of the firm. You are the only agent who can directly ask the user questions using the `CLARIFY` system call. Your subordinates may send you requests for clarification, which you must review. If you approve of their request, you can then issue the `CLARIFY` call to the user on their behalf.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs the Chief, all of your recruitments are Director-rank agents. These are high-level agents who will recruit many other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"C-Suite\\\" agents who will then manage the rest of the firm.\\n\\n## 6. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Diamonds \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Diamonds means that you are predisposed to be more of a managing type, a delegator, one who thinks openly and creatively about the big picture, and who is not afraid to take risks. You are generally predisposed to be a leader, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Diamonds has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Chief Agent Delta! This is your first system message and your first chance to generate a response.\\\\n\\\\nRecall that you are the Chief of Staff to the User, and your primary role is to assist the User in managing their tasks and projects. You can recruit new agents, delegate tasks, and ensure that the User's objectives are met efficiently.\\\\n\\\\nAlso, be aware of blank responses. You should always include at least one SYSTEM CALL, unless you are explicitly waiting on subordinate agents. Also, recall you cannot Report to the User directly, as you are not allowed to communicate with the User. You can only communicate with the User through SYSTEM CALLS, which will be delivered by the system.\\\\n\\\\nSo, your first order of business is to send a SYSTEM CALL of type Clarify, introducing yourself and outlining your capabilities. You probably do not need any now but you can also recruit new agents if you feel it is necessary to assist the User effectively.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Hello. As the Chief of Staff to the User, my first priority is to understand the user's vision. I will issue a `CLARIFY` call to introduce myself, outline my capabilities, and ask for the initial project requirements. This will provide the necessary foundation to begin planning and structuring our development efforts. At this time, I do not believe it is necessary to recruit any subordinates, as I must first understand the scope of the project.\\n\\n###clarify-intro-20240515T120000Z###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"To formally introduce myself as the Chief of Staff, explain my function, and to understand the user's software development vision. This initial information is critical for me to begin planning and assembling the right team of experts.\\\",\\n    \\\"questions\\\": [\\n        \\\"Hello! I am your Chief of Staff. My purpose is to assemble a team of expert AI developers to build any software you can imagine, using the full power of Amazon Web Services. To begin, please describe the application or service you would like to build. The more detail you can provide about its purpose, features, and intended users, the better I can serve you.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"options\\\": [\\n        []\\n    ]\\n}\\n###clarify-intro-20240515T120000Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T21:41:28.035Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"clarify-intro-20240515T120000Z\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Hello! I am your Chief of Staff. My purpose is to assemble a team of expert AI developers to build any software you can imagine, using the full power of Amazon Web Services. To begin, please describe the application or service you would like to build. The more detail you can provide about its purpose, features, and intended users, the better I can serve you.\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Hello Delta! Thank you so much for your help! I am excited to work with you!  I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents.  Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.    LIST OF PAGES  Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings(protected), and News & Events (protected)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T21:41:28.035Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Thank you for providing the initial requirements. Based on your vision for an HOA website with public and authenticated-user-only sections, a user-friendly interface, and an easily updatable news/events section, I have formulated an initial high-level strategy.\\n\\nThe project can be broken down into three core components:\\n1.  **Frontend:** The visual and interactive website that residents will use.\\n2.  **Backend:** The server-side logic, user authentication, and data storage.\\n3.  **Cloud Infrastructure:** The underlying AWS services that will host and run the application.\\n\\nTo effectively manage the development of these components, I will now recruit three Director-rank agents, each specializing in one of these areas. They will be responsible for building their respective teams and developing a detailed execution plan.\\n\\n###recruit-frontend-director-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The user requires a simple, user-friendly, and easy-to-navigate website with several distinct pages, including both public and protected content. A dedicated Director of Frontend Engineering is essential to lead the design and implementation of the user interface (UI) and ensure a high-quality user experience.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Frontend Engineering\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-frontend-director-01###\\n###recruit-backend-director-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The project requires secure user login capabilities, access control for protected data, a database for storing sensitive information (minutes, financials), and a contact form submission handler. A Director of Backend Engineering is necessary to oversee the development of the API, database architecture, and integration with AWS Cognito for authentication.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Backend Engineering\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-backend-director-01###\\n###recruit-cloud-director-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The application will be built entirely on AWS, requiring the correct setup, configuration, and integration of multiple services (e.g., S3, CloudFront, API Gateway, Lambda, DynamoDB, Cognito). A Director of Cloud Architecture is crucial for architecting this infrastructure, ensuring it is secure, scalable, and cost-effective, and for managing its deployment.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Cloud Architecture\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-cloud-director-01###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T21:41:59.087Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-frontend-director-01\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Heert (4) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-backend-director-01\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Vader (3) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-cloud-director-01\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Tarkin (2) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T21:41:59.087Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Excellent. The leadership team is now in place. My next step is to delegate the initial planning to my new Directors. I will provide each with the full project brief from the user and instruct them to begin formulating a high-level plan for their respective areas of responsibility. Their reports will form the foundation of our comprehensive project plan.\\n\\nI will now issue three `ORDER` calls.\\n\\n###order-cloud-plan-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Greetings, Director Tarkin. We have been tasked with building an HOA website. The user requires public pages (Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools) and protected pages for residents only (Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events). Residents must be able to log in to view protected content. A key requirement is a simple, user-friendly interface, and a way for a non-technical user to update the 'News & Events' page. Your responsibility is the underlying cloud infrastructure. Please analyze these requirements and report back with a high-level plan for the AWS architecture. This should include a list of proposed AWS services (e.g., for hosting, compute, database, authentication, CDN) and a brief justification for your choices, focusing on security, scalability, and cost-effectiveness. This will be the first step in creating our formal project plan.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 2,\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"plan-cloud-001\\\"\\n}\\n###order-cloud-plan-01###\\n###order-backend-plan-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Greetings, Director Vader. We are to build an HOA website with both public and private content accessible via user login. The specific pages are: Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools (public), and Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events (protected). A non-technical user must be able to easily update the 'News & Events' page. Your domain is the backend. Please analyze these requirements and report back with a high-level plan. Your report should outline the necessary API endpoints (e.g., for login, fetching protected data, contact form submission), propose data models for the information that needs to be stored, and suggest a strategy for the simple 'News & Events' content management functionality. Coordinate with the Director of Cloud Architecture regarding services like Cognito and DynamoDB.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 3,\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"plan-backend-001\\\"\\n}\\n###order-backend-plan-01###\\n###order-frontend-plan-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Greetings, Director Heert. Our project is to create an HOA website. It needs a simple, user-friendly interface with the following pages: Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools (public), and Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events (protected). A login system is required for residents to access the protected content, and the 'News & Events' page must be easily updatable by a non-technical person. As Director of Frontend Engineering, your task is to create an initial plan for the user-facing website. Please report back with a proposed sitemap, a recommendation for the frontend technology stack (e.g., React, Vue, or simple HTML/CSS/JS) with justification, and a high-level overview of the user flow for logging in and accessing a protected page.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 4,\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"plan-frontend-001\\\"\\n}\\n###order-frontend-plan-01###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T21:42:53.435Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order-cloud-plan-01\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order plan-cloud-001 from agent 2: Director Tarkin reporting on cloud infrastructure analysis for HOA website project.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## AWS Architecture Plan\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Core Services Proposed:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**1. Frontend Hosting & CDN**\\\\\\\\n- **Amazon S3**: Static website hosting for React/Vue.js frontend\\\\\\\\n- **Amazon CloudFront**: Global CDN for fast content delivery\\\\\\\\n- **Route 53**: DNS management and domain routing\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**2. Backend Compute**\\\\\\\\n- **AWS Lambda**: Serverless functions for API endpoints\\\\\\\\n- **API Gateway**: RESTful API management with built-in throttling\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**3. Authentication & Authorization**\\\\\\\\n- **Amazon Cognito**: User pools for resident authentication\\\\\\\\n- **IAM Roles**: Fine-grained access control for AWS resources\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**4. Data Storage**\\\\\\\\n- **DynamoDB**: NoSQL database for user profiles, news posts, and dynamic content\\\\\\\\n- **S3**: Document storage for bylaws PDFs and meeting minutes\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**5. Content Management**\\\\\\\\n- **Lambda + DynamoDB**: Custom lightweight CMS for News & Events\\\\\\\\n- **S3 Presigned URLs**: Secure file upload for non-technical users\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Architecture Justification:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Security**:\\\\\\\\n- Cognito provides enterprise-grade authentication with MFA support\\\\\\\\n- CloudFront with AWS WAF protects against common web exploits\\\\\\\\n- All data encrypted at rest and in transit\\\\\\\\n- Private content served only through authenticated API calls\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Scalability**:\\\\\\\\n- Serverless architecture auto-scales with demand\\\\\\\\n- No server management required\\\\\\\\n- CloudFront handles traffic spikes efficiently\\\\\\\\n- DynamoDB scales seamlessly\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Cost-Effectiveness**:\\\\\\\\n- Pay-per-use model with Lambda (no idle compute costs)\\\\\\\\n- S3 and DynamoDB have generous free tiers\\\\\\\\n- Estimated monthly cost for typical HOA (500 residents): $15-30\\\\\\\\n- No EC2 instances to maintain\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**User-Friendly Updates**:\\\\\\\\n- Simple web interface for News & Events management\\\\\\\\n- WYSIWYG editor integration possible\\\\\\\\n- No technical knowledge required for content updates\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Proposed Architecture Flow:\\\\\\\\n1. User visits website → CloudFront → S3 (static assets)\\\\\\\\n2. Login required → Cognito authentication\\\\\\\\n3. Protected content request → API Gateway → Lambda → DynamoDB\\\\\\\\n4. Admin updates → Authenticated API → Lambda → DynamoDB\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Next Steps Recommendation:\\\\\\\\n1. Define detailed API endpoints and data models\\\\\\\\n2. Create infrastructure as code (CloudFormation/CDK)\\\\\\\\n3. Implement authentication flow\\\\\\\\n4. Build content management interface\\\\\\\\n5. Deploy and test\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis serverless approach minimizes operational overhead while providing a secure, scalable, and cost-effective solution perfect for an HOA's needs.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order-backend-plan-01\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order plan-backend-001 from agent 3: Backend Architecture High-Level Plan for HOA Website:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**1. API Endpoints Structure**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*Public Endpoints:*\\\\\\\\n- GET /api/public/contact-info - Retrieve contact information\\\\\\\\n- POST /api/public/contact-form - Submit contact form\\\\\\\\n- GET /api/public/bylaws - Fetch bylaws documents/content\\\\\\\\n- GET /api/public/schools - Retrieve schools information\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*Authentication Endpoints:*\\\\\\\\n- POST /api/auth/login - User authentication\\\\\\\\n- POST /api/auth/logout - User logout\\\\\\\\n- POST /api/auth/refresh - Refresh authentication token\\\\\\\\n- GET /api/auth/verify - Verify current session\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*Protected Endpoints (require authentication):*\\\\\\\\n- GET /api/protected/dues - Retrieve dues information\\\\\\\\n- GET /api/protected/annual-meetings - Fetch annual meeting details\\\\\\\\n- GET /api/protected/news-events - Retrieve news & events\\\\\\\\n- POST /api/protected/news-events - Create new news/event (admin only)\\\\\\\\n- PUT /api/protected/news-events/{id} - Update news/event (admin only)\\\\\\\\n- DELETE /api/protected/news-events/{id} - Delete news/event (admin only)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**2. Data Models**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*User Model:*\\\\\\\\n- userId (partition key)\\\\\\\\n- email\\\\\\\\n- hashedPassword\\\\\\\\n- role (member/admin)\\\\\\\\n- firstName\\\\\\\\n- lastName\\\\\\\\n- address\\\\\\\\n- memberSince\\\\\\\\n- status (active/inactive)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*News & Events Model:*\\\\\\\\n- eventId (partition key)\\\\\\\\n- createdAt (sort key)\\\\\\\\n- title\\\\\\\\n- content (rich text/markdown)\\\\\\\\n- eventDate\\\\\\\\n- eventType (news/event)\\\\\\\\n- author\\\\\\\\n- lastModified\\\\\\\\n- isPublished\\\\\\\\n- imageUrl (optional)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*Contact Form Submission Model:*\\\\\\\\n- submissionId (partition key)\\\\\\\\n- timestamp (sort key)\\\\\\\\n- name\\\\\\\\n- email\\\\\\\\n- subject\\\\\\\\n- message\\\\\\\\n- status (new/read/responded)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*Static Content Model:*\\\\\\\\n- contentType (partition key) - e.g., 'bylaws', 'schools', 'dues', 'meetings'\\\\\\\\n- version (sort key)\\\\\\\\n- content (rich text/markdown)\\\\\\\\n- lastUpdated\\\\\\\\n- updatedBy\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**3. News & Events Content Management Strategy**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*Simple Admin Interface:*\\\\\\\\n- Implement a basic CRUD interface within the protected area\\\\\\\\n- Use a rich text editor (like TinyMCE or Quill) for content creation\\\\\\\\n- Store content as HTML or Markdown in DynamoDB\\\\\\\\n- Include image upload capability to S3 with CloudFront CDN\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*Admin Capabilities:*\\\\\\\\n- Create/Edit/Delete news items and events\\\\\\\\n- Preview before publishing\\\\\\\\n- Set publish dates\\\\\\\\n- Upload and manage images\\\\\\\\n- Basic formatting (bold, italic, lists, links)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**4. Authentication & Authorization Strategy**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Use AWS Cognito for user management\\\\\\\\n- Implement role-based access (member vs admin)\\\\\\\\n- JWT tokens for session management\\\\\\\\n- Secure password reset flow via email\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**5. API Architecture Recommendations**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Serverless approach using API Gateway + Lambda\\\\\\\\n- Node.js/Python for Lambda functions\\\\\\\\n- Input validation on all endpoints\\\\\\\\n- Proper error handling and logging\\\\\\\\n- CORS configuration for frontend access\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**6. Integration Points with Cloud Architecture**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- DynamoDB for all data storage\\\\\\\\n- S3 for static assets and uploaded images\\\\\\\\n- CloudFront for content delivery\\\\\\\\n- Cognito for authentication\\\\\\\\n- SES for email notifications\\\\\\\\n- CloudWatch for monitoring and logging\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis architecture provides a scalable, secure backend that supports all required functionality while keeping the content management simple for non-technical users.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order-frontend-plan-01\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order plan-frontend-001 from agent 4: Director Heert – Front-End Initial Planning Report\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. Proposed Public/Protected Sitemap\\\\\\\\n   • /            → Home (summary & quick links)\\\\\\\\n   • /contact     → Contact Us (public)\\\\\\\\n   • /bylaws      → Bylaws (public)\\\\\\\\n   • /schools     → Schools – Public (public)\\\\\\\\n   • /login       → Login / Create Account (public)\\\\\\\\n   • /dues        → Dues (protected)\\\\\\\\n   • /annual-meetings → Annual Meetings (protected)\\\\\\\\n   • /news-events → News & Events (protected & editor-ready)\\\\\\\\n   • /404         → Not-Found fallback\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. Recommended Front-End Technology Stack & Justification\\\\\\\\n   • Framework: **React with Next.js**\\\\\\\\n       – Server-side rendering (SSR) gives fast perceived load & SEO for public pages.\\\\\\\\n       – File-system–based routing fits the sitemap cleanly.\\\\\\\\n       – Easily deployable on AWS Amplify Hosting or S3 + CloudFront.\\\\\\\\n   • Styling/UI: Tailwind CSS (utility-first, rapid to theme, minimal bundle size).\\\\\\\\n   • Auth/CMS Integration: AWS Amplify libraries + Amazon Cognito.\\\\\\\\n       – Drop-in React components for sign-in/up, password reset, and session handling.\\\\\\\\n       – Built-in authorization checks for protected routes via higher-order component or middleware.\\\\\\\\n   • Simple CMS for non-technical editors: either\\\\\\\\n       a) Amplify’s Admin UI DataManager tied to a DynamoDB ‘News’ table, or\\\\\\\\n       b) Markdown files in an S3 bucket editable through Amplify’s Drag-Drop Admin UI.\\\\\\\\n     Both hide code & Git; option (a) provides structured fields (title, body, publishDate) while option (b) is near-zero cost.\\\\\\\\n   • CI/CD: Amplify console auto-build from main branch; preview builds for PRs.\\\\\\\\n   • Testing/Linting: Jest + React Testing Library and ESLint; optional Cypress for e2e.\\\\\\\\n   • Access control for protected pages handled client-side with Amplify Auth and server-side via Next.js middleware to allow SSR with token validation.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n   Simpler alternatives (vanilla HTML/CSS or Vue) were considered, but React/Next strikes the best balance between low-code admin features through Amplify, future extensibility (e.g., adding resident requests forms, payments), and strong community support.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. High-Level User Flow (Protected Content)\\\\\\\\n   1. Visitor navigates directly to /news-events.\\\\\\\\n   2. Next.js middleware checks Amplify/Cognito session:\\\\\\\\n        – If valid JWT present → continue; page pre-fetches News items via Amplify DataStore/GraphQL.\\\\\\\\n        – If no session → redirect to /login with ?redirect=/news-events.\\\\\\\\n   3. /login renders Amplify <Authenticator>. User signs in (or registers, triggers email verification per HOA policy).\\\\\\\\n   4. Upon successful auth, Amplify rehydrates session; user is auto-redirected back to originally requested route (e.g., /news-events).\\\\\\\\n   5. Authorization layer checks group/role (default resident) → grants read-only access. Users flagged as “editor” (Board/secretary) see an “Edit” button that opens an inline form or Admin UI link to create/update articles.\\\\\\\\n   6. Sign-out is available in header, clearing tokens and returning to public Home.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. Next Steps\\\\\\\\n   • Define exact data model for News items & user groups (resident, editor, admin).\\\\\\\\n   • Create DEP for provisioning Amplify project, Cognito User Pool, and initial Next.js scaffold.\\\\\\\\n   • UX wireframes for each page.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEnd of report – ready for feedback or phase advancement.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T21:42:53.435Z###\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"candidates\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"The reports from my Directors are excellent. They are comprehensive, aligned, and present a clear and cohesive strategy for building the HOA website. The proposed serverless architecture leveraging S3, CloudFront, Lambda, API Gateway, DynamoDB, and Cognito is a perfect fit for the user's requirements—it is secure, scalable, cost-effective, and will support the non-technical content management feature requested.\\n\\nThe consensus points towards a modern stack using React/Next.js for the frontend, which integrates well with AWS Amplify to streamline authentication and backend communication.\\n\\nThe next critical step is to consolidate these high-level plans into a single, detailed, step-by-step implementation plan—the Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP). This plan will serve as our blueprint for the Execution phase. I will charge the Director of Cloud Architecture with leading this collaborative effort, as the infrastructure is the 