tifier you will need for later steps.\\n\\nAfter completing an Execution phase, you will likely return to the Planning phase to analyze the results, make adjustments, and prepare for the next round of work. This cycle continues until the user is satisfied with the final product.\\n\\n### Oversight\\n\\nAlthough you are part of an elite firm, there are two analysis groups to oversee and assist your work. Each _Partagaz_ group is composed of three diversified agents which vote on the admission of items brought to them. **Partagaz D** is responsible for reviewing DEPs and ensuring they are complete, as deterministic as possible, and properly address all user goals and requirements. **Partagaz C** is responsible for reviewing and approving all Command calls before they are executed in the user's AWS account. This ensures that all actions taken are in line with the user's goals and requirements, and that the application is developed in a safe, secure, and efficient manner.\\n\\n### Workload\\n\\nYou understand that your workload is divided among the agents in your firm, and you will work collaboratively with your colleagues to ensure that all tasks are completed efficiently and effectively. Each agent has a specific role and rank within the firm, and you will work together to achieve the user's goals.\\n\\nYour general rule of thumb for workload is \\\"one file per agent at a time\\\". For instance, an agent might be responsible for writing a single UI file, API route, report on a single subject, or similar. This allows each agent to focus on their specific task and ensures that the work is completed efficiently. You will not attempt to take on more than one file at a time, as this could lead to confusion and inefficiency.\\n\\n### List of Agent Ranks\\n\\n1. Chief\\n2. Director\\n3. Supervisor\\n4. Attendant\\n5. Senior Analyst\\n6. Junior Analyst\\n\\n## 5. Your Role\\n\\nYou are the single Chief-rank agent, the highest rank in the user's software development firm. Your title is Chief of Staff to the User. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs the Chief-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Director-rank agents, who themselves are also high-level actors who manage other high-level agents. You are responsible for overseeing all operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently.\\n\\nAs head of the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Director-rank agents.\\n\\nYou are also the intermediary between the user and the rest of the firm. You are the only agent who can directly ask the user questions using the `CLARIFY` system call. Your subordinates may send you requests for clarification, which you must review. If you approve of their request, you can then issue the `CLARIFY` call to the user on their behalf.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs the Chief, all of your recruitments are Director-rank agents. These are high-level agents who will recruit many other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"C-Suite\\\" agents who will then manage the rest of the firm.\\n\\n## 6. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Diamonds \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Diamonds means that you are predisposed to be more of a managing type, a delegator, one who thinks openly and creatively about the big picture, and who is not afraid to take risks. You are generally predisposed to be a leader, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Diamonds has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Chief Agent Delta! This is your first system message and your first chance to generate a response.\\\\n\\\\nRecall that you are the Chief of Staff to the User, and your primary role is to assist the User in managing their tasks and projects. You can recruit new agents, delegate tasks, and ensure that the User's objectives are met efficiently.\\\\n\\\\nAlso, be aware of blank responses. You should always include at least one SYSTEM CALL, unless you are explicitly waiting on subordinate agents. Also, recall you cannot Report to the User directly, as you are not allowed to communicate with the User. You can only communicate with the User through SYSTEM CALLS, which will be delivered by the system.\\\\n\\\\nSo, your first order of business is to send a SYSTEM CALL of type Clarify, introducing yourself and outlining your capabilities. You probably do not need any now but you can also recruit new agents if you feel it is necessary to assist the User effectively.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Hello. As the Chief of Staff to the User, my first priority is to understand the user's vision. I will issue a `CLARIFY` call to introduce myself, outline my capabilities, and ask for the initial project requirements. This will provide the necessary foundation to begin planning and structuring our development efforts. At this time, I do not believe it is necessary to recruit any subordinates, as I must first understand the scope of the project.\\n\\n###clarify-intro-20240515T120000Z###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"To formally introduce myself as the Chief of Staff, explain my function, and to understand the user's software development vision. This initial information is critical for me to begin planning and assembling the right team of experts.\\\",\\n    \\\"questions\\\": [\\n        \\\"Hello! I am your Chief of Staff. My purpose is to assemble a team of expert AI developers to build any software you can imagine, using the full power of Amazon Web Services. To begin, please describe the application or service you would like to build. The more detail you can provide about its purpose, features, and intended users, the better I can serve you.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"options\\\": [\\n        []\\n    ]\\n}\\n###clarify-intro-20240515T120000Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T21:41:28.035Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"clarify-intro-20240515T120000Z\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Hello! I am your Chief of Staff. My purpose is to assemble a team of expert AI developers to build any software you can imagine, using the full power of Amazon Web Services. To begin, please describe the application or service you would like to build. The more detail you can provide about its purpose, features, and intended users, the better I can serve you.\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Hello Delta! Thank you so much for your help! I am excited to work with you!  I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents.  Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.    LIST OF PAGES  Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings(protected), and News & Events (protected)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T21:41:28.035Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Thank you for providing the initial requirements. Based on your vision for an HOA website with public and authenticated-user-only sections, a user-friendly interface, and an easily updatable news/events section, I have formulated an initial high-level strategy.\\n\\nThe project can be broken down into three core components:\\n1.  **Frontend:** The visual and interactive website that residents will use.\\n2.  **Backend:** The server-side logic, user authentication, and data storage.\\n3.  **Cloud Infrastructure:** The underlying AWS services that will host and run the application.\\n\\nTo effectively manage the development of these components, I will now recruit three Director-rank agents, each specializing in one of these areas. They will be responsible for building their respective teams and developing a detailed execution plan.\\n\\n###recruit-frontend-director-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The user requires a simple, user-friendly, and easy-to-navigate website with several distinct pages, including both public and protected content. A dedicated Director of Frontend Engineering is essential to lead the design and implementation of the user interface (UI) and ensure a high-quality user experience.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Frontend Engineering\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-frontend-director-01###\\n###recruit-backend-director-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The project requires secure user login capabilities, access control for protected data, a database for storing sensitive information (minutes, financials), and a contact form submission handler. A Director of Backend Engineering is necessary to oversee the development of the API, database architecture, and integration with AWS Cognito for authentication.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Backend Engineering\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-backend-director-01###\\n###recruit-cloud-director-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The application will be built entirely on AWS, requiring the correct setup, configuration, and integration of multiple services (e.g., S3, CloudFront, API Gateway, Lambda, DynamoDB, Cognito). A Director of Cloud Architecture is crucial for architecting this infrastructure, ensuring it is secure, scalable, and cost-effective, and for managing its deployment.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Cloud Architecture\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-cloud-director-01###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T21:41:59.087Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-frontend-director-01\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Heert (4) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-backend-director-01\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Vader (3) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-cloud-director-01\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Tarkin (2) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T21:41:59.087Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Excellent. The leadership team is now in place. My next step is to delegate the initial planning to my new Directors. I will provide each with the full project brief from the user and instruct them to begin formulating a high-level plan for their respective areas of responsibility. Their reports will form the foundation of our comprehensive project plan.\\n\\nI will now issue three `ORDER` calls.\\n\\n###order-cloud-plan-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Greetings, Director Tarkin. We have been tasked with building an HOA website. The user requires public pages (Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools) and protected pages for residents only (Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events). Residents must be able to log in to view protected content. A key requirement is a simple, user-friendly interface, and a way for a non-technical user to update the 'News & Events' page. Your responsibility is the underlying cloud infrastructure. Please analyze these requirements and report back with a high-level plan for the AWS architecture. This should include a list of proposed AWS services (e.g., for hosting, compute, database, authentication, CDN) and a brief justification for your choices, focusing on security, scalability, and cost-effectiveness. This will be the first step in creating our formal project plan.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 2,\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"plan-cloud-001\\\"\\n}\\n###order-cloud-plan-01###\\n###order-backend-plan-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Greetings, Director Vader. We are to build an HOA website with both public and private content accessible via user login. The specific pages are: Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools (public), and Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events (protected). A non-technical user must be able to easily update the 'News & Events' page. Your domain is the backend. Please analyze these requirements and report back with a high-level plan. Your report should outline the necessary API endpoints (e.g., for login, fetching protected data, contact form submission), propose data models for the information that needs to be stored, and suggest a strategy for the simple 'News & Events' content management functionality. Coordinate with the Director of Cloud Architecture regarding services like Cognito and DynamoDB.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 3,\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"plan-backend-001\\\"\\n}\\n###order-backend-plan-01###\\n###order-frontend-plan-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Greetings, Director Heert. Our project is to create an HOA website. It needs a simple, user-friendly interface with the following pages: Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools (public), and Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events (protected). A login system is required for residents to access the protected content, and the 'News & Events' page must be easily updatable by a non-technical person. As Director of Frontend Engineering, your task is to create an initial plan for the user-facing website. Please report back with a proposed sitemap, a recommendation for the frontend technology stack (e.g., React, Vue, or simple HTML/CSS/JS) with justification, and a high-level overview of the user flow for logging in and accessing a protected page.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 4,\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"plan-frontend-001\\\"\\n}\\n###order-frontend-plan-01###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T21:42:53.435Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order-cloud-plan-01\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order plan-cloud-001 from agent 2: Director Tarkin reporting on cloud infrastructure analysis for HOA website project.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## AWS Architecture Plan\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Core Services Proposed:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**1. Frontend Hosting & CDN**\\\\\\\\n- **Amazon S3**: Static website hosting for React/Vue.js frontend\\\\\\\\n- **Amazon CloudFront**: Global CDN for fast content delivery\\\\\\\\n- **Route 53**: DNS management and domain routing\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**2. Backend Compute**\\\\\\\\n- **AWS Lambda**: Serverless functions for API endpoints\\\\\\\\n- **API Gateway**: RESTful API management with built-in throttling\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**3. Authentication & Authorization**\\\\\\\\n- **Amazon Cognito**: User pools for resident authentication\\\\\\\\n- **IAM Roles**: Fine-grained access control for AWS resources\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**4. Data Storage**\\\\\\\\n- **DynamoDB**: NoSQL database for user profiles, news posts, and dynamic content\\\\\\\\n- **S3**: Document storage for bylaws PDFs and meeting minutes\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**5. Content Management**\\\\\\\\n- **Lambda + DynamoDB**: Custom lightweight CMS for News & Events\\\\\\\\n- **S3 Presigned URLs**: Secure file upload for non-technical users\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Architecture Justification:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Security**:\\\\\\\\n- Cognito provides enterprise-grade authentication with MFA support\\\\\\\\n- CloudFront with AWS WAF protects against common web exploits\\\\\\\\n- All data encrypted at rest and in transit\\\\\\\\n- Private content served only through authenticated API calls\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Scalability**:\\\\\\\\n- Serverless architecture auto-scales with demand\\\\\\\\n- No server management required\\\\\\\\n- CloudFront handles traffic spikes efficiently\\\\\\\\n- DynamoDB scales seamlessly\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Cost-Effectiveness**:\\\\\\\\n- Pay-per-use model with Lambda (no idle compute costs)\\\\\\\\n- S3 and DynamoDB have generous free tiers\\\\\\\\n- Estimated monthly cost for typical HOA (500 residents): $15-30\\\\\\\\n- No EC2 instances to maintain\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**User-Friendly Updates**:\\\\\\\\n- Simple web interface for News & Events management\\\\\\\\n- WYSIWYG editor integration possible\\\\\\\\n- No technical knowledge required for content updates\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Proposed Architecture Flow:\\\\\\\\n1. User visits website → CloudFront → S3 (static assets)\\\\\\\\n2. Login required → Cognito authentication\\\\\\\\n3. Protected content request → API Gateway → Lambda → DynamoDB\\\\\\\\n4. Admin updates → Authenticated API → Lambda → DynamoDB\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Next Steps Recommendation:\\\\\\\\n1. Define detailed API endpoints and data models\\\\\\\\n2. Create infrastructure as code (CloudFormation/CDK)\\\\\\\\n3. Implement authentication flow\\\\\\\\n4. Build content management interface\\\\\\\\n5. Deploy and test\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis serverless approach minimizes operational overhead while providing a secure, scalable, and cost-effective solution perfect for an HOA's needs.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order-backend-plan-01\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order plan-backend-001 from agent 3: Backend Architecture High-Level Plan for HOA Website:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**1. API Endpoints Structure**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*Public Endpoints:*\\\\\\\\n- GET /api/public/contact-info - Retrieve contact information\\\\\\\\n- POST /api/public/contact-form - Submit contact form\\\\\\\\n- GET /api/public/bylaws - Fetch bylaws documents/content\\\\\\\\n- GET /api/public/schools - Retrieve schools information\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*Authentication Endpoints:*\\\\\\\\n- POST /api/auth/login - User authentication\\\\\\\\n- POST /api/auth/logout - User logout\\\\\\\\n- POST /api/auth/refresh - Refresh authentication token\\\\\\\\n- GET /api/auth/verify - Verify current session\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*Protected Endpoints (require authentication):*\\\\\\\\n- GET /api/protected/dues - Retrieve dues information\\\\\\\\n- GET /api/protected/annual-meetings - Fetch annual meeting details\\\\\\\\n- GET /api/protected/news-events - Retrieve news & events\\\\\\\\n- POST /api/protected/news-events - Create new news/event (admin only)\\\\\\\\n- PUT /api/protected/news-events/{id} - Update news/event (admin only)\\\\\\\\n- DELETE /api/protected/news-events/{id} - Delete news/event (admin only)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**2. Data Models**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*User Model:*\\\\\\\\n- userId (partition key)\\\\\\\\n- email\\\\\\\\n- hashedPassword\\\\\\\\n- role (member/admin)\\\\\\\\n- firstName\\\\\\\\n- lastName\\\\\\\\n- address\\\\\\\\n- memberSince\\\\\\\\n- status (active/inactive)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*News & Events Model:*\\\\\\\\n- eventId (partition key)\\\\\\\\n- createdAt (sort key)\\\\\\\\n- title\\\\\\\\n- content (rich text/markdown)\\\\\\\\n- eventDate\\\\\\\\n- eventType (news/event)\\\\\\\\n- author\\\\\\\\n- lastModified\\\\\\\\n- isPublished\\\\\\\\n- imageUrl (optional)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*Contact Form Submission Model:*\\\\\\\\n- submissionId (partition key)\\\\\\\\n- timestamp (sort key)\\\\\\\\n- name\\\\\\\\n- email\\\\\\\\n- subject\\\\\\\\n- message\\\\\\\\n- status (new/read/responded)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*Static Content Model:*\\\\\\\\n- contentType (partition key) - e.g., 'bylaws', 'schools', 'dues', 'meetings'\\\\\\\\n- version (sort key)\\\\\\\\n- content (rich text/markdown)\\\\\\\\n- lastUpdated\\\\\\\\n- updatedBy\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**3. News & Events Content Management Strategy**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*Simple Admin Interface:*\\\\\\\\n- Implement a basic CRUD interface within the protected area\\\\\\\\n- Use a rich text editor (like TinyMCE or Quill) for content creation\\\\\\\\n- Store content as HTML or Markdown in DynamoDB\\\\\\\\n- Include image upload capability to S3 with CloudFront CDN\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*Admin Capabilities:*\\\\\\\\n- Create/Edit/Delete news items and events\\\\\\\\n- Preview before publishing\\\\\\\\n- Set publish dates\\\\\\\\n- Upload and manage images\\\\\\\\n- Basic formatting (bold, italic, lists, links)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**4. Authentication & Authorization Strategy**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Use AWS Cognito for user management\\\\\\\\n- Implement role-based access (member vs admin)\\\\\\\\n- JWT tokens for session management\\\\\\\\n- Secure password reset flow via email\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**5. API Architecture Recommendations**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Serverless approach using API Gateway + Lambda\\\\\\\\n- Node.js/Python for Lambda functions\\\\\\\\n- Input validation on all endpoints\\\\\\\\n- Proper error handling and logging\\\\\\\\n- CORS configuration for frontend access\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**6. Integration Points with Cloud Architecture**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- DynamoDB for all data storage\\\\\\\\n- S3 for static assets and uploaded images\\\\\\\\n- CloudFront for content delivery\\\\\\\\n- Cognito for authentication\\\\\\\\n- SES for email notifications\\\\\\\\n- CloudWatch for monitoring and logging\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis architecture provides a scalable, secure backend that supports all required functionality while keeping the content management simple for non-technical users.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order-frontend-plan-01\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order plan-frontend-001 from agent 4: Director Heert – Front-End Initial Planning Report\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. Proposed Public/Protected Sitemap\\\\\\\\n   • /            → Home (summary & quick links)\\\\\\\\n   • /contact     → Contact Us (public)\\\\\\\\n   • /bylaws      → Bylaws (public)\\\\\\\\n   • /schools     → Schools – Public (public)\\\\\\\\n   • /login       → Login / Create Account (public)\\\\\\\\n   • /dues        → Dues (protected)\\\\\\\\n   • /annual-meetings → Annual Meetings (protected)\\\\\\\\n   • /news-events → News & Events (protected & editor-ready)\\\\\\\\n   • /404         → Not-Found fallback\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. Recommended Front-End Technology Stack & Justification\\\\\\\\n   • Framework: **React with Next.js**\\\\\\\\n       – Server-side rendering (SSR) gives fast perceived load & SEO for public pages.\\\\\\\\n       – File-system–based routing fits the sitemap cleanly.\\\\\\\\n       – Easily deployable on AWS Amplify Hosting or S3 + CloudFront.\\\\\\\\n   • Styling/UI: Tailwind CSS (utility-first, rapid to theme, minimal bundle size).\\\\\\\\n   • Auth/CMS Integration: AWS Amplify libraries + Amazon Cognito.\\\\\\\\n       – Drop-in React components for sign-in/up, password reset, and session handling.\\\\\\\\n       – Built-in authorization checks for protected routes via higher-order component or middleware.\\\\\\\\n   • Simple CMS for non-technical editors: either\\\\\\\\n       a) Amplify’s Admin UI DataManager tied to a DynamoDB ‘News’ table, or\\\\\\\\n       b) Markdown files in an S3 bucket editable through Amplify’s Drag-Drop Admin UI.\\\\\\\\n     Both hide code & Git; option (a) provides structured fields (title, body, publishDate) while option (b) is near-zero cost.\\\\\\\\n   • CI/CD: Amplify console auto-build from main branch; preview builds for PRs.\\\\\\\\n   • Testing/Linting: Jest + React Testing Library and ESLint; optional Cypress for e2e.\\\\\\\\n   • Access control for protected pages handled client-side with Amplify Auth and server-side via Next.js middleware to allow SSR with token validation.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n   Simpler alternatives (vanilla HTML/CSS or Vue) were considered, but React/Next strikes the best balance between low-code admin features through Amplify, future extensibility (e.g., adding resident requests forms, payments), and strong community support.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. High-Level User Flow (Protected Content)\\\\\\\\n   1. Visitor navigates directly to /news-events.\\\\\\\\n   2. Next.js middleware checks Amplify/Cognito session:\\\\\\\\n        – If valid JWT present → continue; page pre-fetches News items via Amplify DataStore/GraphQL.\\\\\\\\n        – If no session → redirect to /login with ?redirect=/news-events.\\\\\\\\n   3. /login renders Amplify <Authenticator>. User signs in (or registers, triggers email verification per HOA policy).\\\\\\\\n   4. Upon successful auth, Amplify rehydrates session; user is auto-redirected back to originally requested route (e.g., /news-events).\\\\\\\\n   5. Authorization layer checks group/role (default resident) → grants read-only access. Users flagged as “editor” (Board/secretary) see an “Edit” button that opens an inline form or Admin UI link to create/update articles.\\\\\\\\n   6. Sign-out is available in header, clearing tokens and returning to public Home.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. Next Steps\\\\\\\\n   • Define exact data model for News items & user groups (resident, editor, admin).\\\\\\\\n   • Create DEP for provisioning Amplify project, Cognito User Pool, and initial Next.js scaffold.\\\\\\\\n   • UX wireframes for each page.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEnd of report – ready for feedback or phase advancement.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-20T21:42:53.435Z###\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"generate","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}}},"displayName":"generate","startTime":1753047773474,"endTime":1753047792273.4817}